0.4fc0ec36acae796600191f045615af67b09e6afa.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:29PM MST until November 6 at 12:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Warning\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\n.Minor flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is expected due\nto upstream flooding occurring in the vicinity of Monte Vista.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon to late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 2:30 PM MST Monday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage early\nWednesday afternoon to a crest of 9.6 feet late Wednesday\nevening. It will then fall below flood stage early Thursday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-06T00:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-05T17:16:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 051716 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1016 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Early morning showers dry out by late morning today, with dry conditions thereafter. - Warmer and drier conditions return for the first part of next week. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH TONIGHT/... Issued at 1247 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026 Today - Tonight: Active weather is e","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD